<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Two miners killed in accident at Dries.</title>
<headline>Two miners killed in accident at Dries.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two mineworkers were killed on Thursday in an underground accident at Driefontein Consolidated Ltd's east division, mine managers Gold Fields of South Africa Ltd said in a statement.</p>
<p>The two mineworkers were killed after a fall of ground 1,700 metres underground in the area served by No 2 shaft, it said.</p>
<p>The accident occurred at about 0700 GMT.</p>
<p>East Driefontien produced 5,754 kg of gold in the three months to end December.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
